# What must NEVER reach the image.
#
# `COPY . .` copies the build context, and the context is the working tree — .gitignore
# has no say in it. Without this file the deployed image carried .env (every production
# secret in plaintext), key.md, the Firebase service-account key under _excluded/, the
# development SQLite database and seven full git worktrees: 1.01 GB of context, ~900 MB
# of it dead weight, and every credential readable by anyone who can pull the image or
# open a console on the machine.
#
# Secrets reach the container through `fly secrets set` (see DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md), never
# through a file in the repository.
#
# HOW THESE MATCH: a pattern is anchored at the context root. `*.log` matches only a
# top-level file; anything at any depth needs `**/`. A pattern that names a directory
# excludes everything under it. `!` re-includes; the last matching line wins.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# The single-server deployment keeps its secrets in deploy/.env, and the two patterns
# above are anchored at the root: they do not match it. Nothing under deploy/ runs
# inside the image (it is the compose file, the Caddyfile and the setup script).
deploy/
**/.env
**/.env.*
key.md
*.pem
*.key
*firebase*adminsdk*.json
_excluded/

# The mobile clients. yalla_gym/ is the Flutter app and the design canvas (1.2 GB);
# mobile/ and flutter/ are abandoned attempts (~2.4 GB together). None of it runs on the
# server, and all of it went into every build context.
yalla_gym/
mobile/
flutter/

# Local databases and developer state
db.sqlite3
*.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
.cursor/
.vscode/
.agent/
.agents/
.venv/
venv/
**/.DS_Store

# Logs. Development writes rotating files under logs/ (django.log.1, diet.log.2, ...),
# which `*.log` never matched, and they hold user email addresses. Production logs go
# to stdout only (settings_production.LOGGING).
logs/
**/*.log
**/*.log.*

# Build and test artifacts. staticfiles/ is REGENERATED by collectstatic during the
# build; copying a local one in would ship stale hashed assets. media/ and
# private_media/ are the development filesystem storage: production media is object
# storage.
staticfiles/
media/
private_media/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# Not part of the running service
tests/
scripts/
docs/
.github/
*.md
!DEPLOY_CHECKLIST.md
# Scratch output at the root of a working tree (plan dumps, comparisons, debug text).
/*.json
/*.txt
!/requirements.txt
